@startuml user_simples

' Módulo user inteiro em um arquivo, no estilo simplista. Os cinco diagramas completos
' continuam em sequencia/user/, um por endpoint.
'
' Três cortes em relação a eles:
'   1. UserRepositoryPort e UserRepositoryImpl viram um participante só, "Repositório".
'   2. Um alt por bloco, o da decisão que define aquele endpoint. Erro de preenchimento
'      (400) e erro de validação de domínio (422) saem, porque se repetem em todos.
'   3. Colaborador sem regra própria vira mensagem para si mesmo, como a codificação da
'      senha, para o fato não sumir junto com a raia.
'
' Os cinco casos de uso continuam como raias separadas: são cinco classes no código, e
' cada bloco usa uma delas.

title Módulo user: os cinco endpoints

actor "Administrador" as Ator
boundary "Frontend" as FE
participant "UserController" as Ctrl
participant "CreateUserUseCase" as Create
participant "GetUserUseCase" as Get
participant "UpdateUserUseCase" as Update
participant "UpdateUserStatusUseCase" as Status
participant "DeleteUserUseCase" as Delete
participant "User" as Entity
participant "Repositório" as Repo
database "users" as DB

== POST /users: criar ==

Ator -> FE: preenche o formulário e confirma
activate FE
FE -> Ctrl: POST /users\n{name, email, password, role}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Create: execute(CreateUserRequest)
activate Create

Create -> Repo: existsByEmail(email)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT COUNT(*)>0 FROM users\nWHERE email=? AND status<>'DELETED'
DB --> Repo: boolean
Repo --> Create: boolean
deactivate Repo

alt email já cadastrado
  Create --> Ctrl: ConflictException
  Ctrl --> FE: 409 Conflict
else email disponível
  Create -> Create: codifica a senha
  Create -> Entity: User.create(name, email, senha, role)
  activate Entity
  Entity -> Entity: id = UUID aleatório\nstatus = ACTIVE
  Entity --> Create: User
  deactivate Entity

  Create -> Repo: save(user)
  activate Repo
  Repo -> DB: INSERT INTO users
  Repo --> Create: User
  deactivate Repo

  Create --> Ctrl: UserResponse
  Ctrl --> FE: 201 Created {UserResponse}
end
deactivate Create
deactivate Ctrl
FE --> Ator: exibe o resultado
deactivate FE

== GET /users e GET /users/{id}: buscar ==

Ator -> FE: abre a lista, ou um usuário
activate FE
FE -> Ctrl: GET /users\nou GET /users/{id}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Get: findAll() ou findById(id)
activate Get

Get -> Repo: findAll() ou findById(UserId.of(id))
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE status<>'DELETED'\n[AND id=?]
DB --> Repo: List<User> ou Optional<User>
Repo --> Get: List<User> ou Optional<User>
deactivate Repo

alt busca por id sem resultado
  Get --> Ctrl: ResourceNotFoundException
  Ctrl --> FE: 404 Not Found
else encontrado
  Get --> Ctrl: UserResponse ou List<UserResponse>
  Ctrl --> FE: 200 OK
end
deactivate Get
deactivate Ctrl
FE --> Ator: exibe o resultado
deactivate FE

== PUT /users/{id}: atualizar ==

Ator -> FE: edita os dados e confirma
activate FE
FE -> Ctrl: PUT /users/{id}\n{name, email, password?, role?}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Update: execute(id, UpdateUserRequest)
activate Update

Update -> Repo: findById(UserId.of(id))
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE id=? AND status<>'DELETED'
DB --> Repo: Optional<User>
Repo --> Update: Optional<User>
deactivate Repo

alt usuário não encontrado
  Update --> Ctrl: ResourceNotFoundException
  Ctrl --> FE: 404 Not Found
else usuário encontrado
  Update -> Update: password em branco mantém a atual\nrole omitida mantém a atual\ncodifica a senha nova, se houver

  Update -> Entity: update(name, email, senha, papel)
  activate Entity
  Entity -> Entity: updatedAt = now()
  Entity --> Update: User
  deactivate Entity

  Update -> Repo: save(user)
  activate Repo
  Repo -> DB: UPDATE users SET\nname=?, email=?, password=?, role=?, updated_at=?
  Repo --> Update: User
  deactivate Repo

  Update --> Ctrl: UserResponse
  Ctrl --> FE: 200 OK {UserResponse}
end
deactivate Update
deactivate Ctrl
FE --> Ator: exibe o resultado
deactivate FE

== PATCH /users/{id}/status: alterar status ==

Ator -> FE: ativa ou desativa o usuário
activate FE
FE -> Ctrl: PATCH /users/{id}/status\n{status: ACTIVE | INACTIVE}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Status: execute(id, request.status())
activate Status

Status -> Repo: findById(UserId.of(id))
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE id=? AND status<>'DELETED'
DB --> Repo: Optional<User>
Repo --> Status: Optional<User>
deactivate Repo

alt status = ACTIVE
  Status -> Entity: activate()
  activate Entity
  Entity --> Status: status = ACTIVE
  deactivate Entity
else status = INACTIVE
  Status -> Entity: deactivate()
  activate Entity
  Entity --> Status: status = INACTIVE
  deactivate Entity
end

Status -> Repo: save(user)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: UPDATE users SET status=?
Repo --> Status: User
deactivate Repo

Status --> Ctrl: UserResponse
deactivate Status
Ctrl --> FE: 200 OK {UserResponse}
deactivate Ctrl
FE --> Ator: exibe o novo status
deactivate FE

== DELETE /users/{id}: remover ==

Ator -> FE: confirma a remoção
activate FE
FE -> Ctrl: DELETE /users/{id}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Delete: execute(id)
activate Delete

Delete -> Repo: findById(UserId.of(id))
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE id=? AND status<>'DELETED'
DB --> Repo: Optional<User>
Repo --> Delete: Optional<User>
deactivate Repo

Delete -> Entity: delete()
activate Entity

alt usuário não está INACTIVE
  Entity --> Delete: InvalidStateException
  Delete --> Ctrl: InvalidStateException
  Ctrl --> FE: 422 Unprocessable Entity\nINVALID_STATE
else usuário INACTIVE
  Entity --> Delete: status = DELETED
  deactivate Entity

  Delete -> Repo: save(user)
  activate Repo
  Repo -> DB: UPDATE users SET status='DELETED'
  Repo --> Delete: User
  deactivate Repo

  Delete --> Ctrl: void
  Ctrl --> FE: 204 No Content
end
deactivate Delete
deactivate Ctrl
FE --> Ator: exibe o resultado
deactivate FE

@enduml
